From 85c9fde4959f15b7e60ed3c656330c8b4bc4aa86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Brotherton <bbrotherton@google.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:43:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "mojo: Use a bespoke protocol for Broker IPC"

This reverts commit 98733539d7007ab84a699f0edf7ff0337fac6dab
(upstream commit 610e7bf531bd, r1737010, crrev.com/c/8616833).

r1737010 replaced Channel::Create() in mojo::core::BrokerHost with a
direct base::IOWatcher read watch that calls recv(..., MSG_DONTWAIT) in
BrokerHost::OnFdReadable() (mojo/core/broker_host.cc). On Linux (glibc),
recv() invokes the recvfrom syscall (__NR_recvfrom, syscall 45 on
x86_64). ChromeOS seccomp policies for daemons hosting Mojo brokers
(such as mojo_service_manager and ml_service) allow read and recvmsg but
do not allow recvfrom, causing mojo_service_manager and ml_service to
crash with SIGSYS (seccomp-violation-recvfrom) and taking down chrome
and shill across VM and hardware tests.

Revert this change in libchrome until ChromeOS daemon seccomp policies
are updated to allow recvfrom (or BrokerHost avoids recv()).

BUG=b:583970032
TEST=sudo emerge libchrome

patch-name: backward-compatibility-2300-Revert-mojo-Use-a-bespoke-protocol-for-Broker-IPC.patch
